:"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Leave it running. In the first terminal, connect using the obtained identity:"},"1499":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Expect HTTP `200`. The client's trust in this local server is its self-signed `consumer.crt`; the server verifies the device against `device-root.pem`. The HTML file displays OpenSSL diagnostic information."},"1500":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"With the same server still running, test that a request without a client certificate is rejected:"},"1501":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Rejection must correspond to a missing certificate at the server, not a stopped server. Stop the consumer with Ctrl+C after the test. This exercise demonstrates TLS authentication and key possession; your application must also define authorization and revocation consumption. Server options are described in openssl-s\\_server."},"1502":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-52/platform/iot