res and retire it when it stops being trustworthy. Lamassu keeps the certificate, its issuing CA, its status and, when it belongs to a device, the identity it is linked to."],[1464,"Issuing root from `device-root.pem`."],[793,"Issuing, binding and installing are separate steps. If an operation fails, check which steps persisted before repeating it."],[1321,"It calls `iot:GetRegistrationCode` to obtain AWS's verification code."],[712,"it can be retrieved by resource, actor and period;"],[2344,"It identifies `device-001`, supports client authentication and verifies against `ca.pem`."],[2342,"It is a CA certificate, is currently valid and its self-signature verifies."],[2150,"It requires the module, token and permissions of the corresponding provider. Check that the Lamassu identifier matches the object accessible from that module. Module configuration belongs to the client environment or Deployment."],[1323,"It sends the CA (in PEM) and the verification certificate to AWS via `iot:RegisterCACertificate`, enabling registration with `AllowAutoRegistration: true`."],[491,"It separately loads the policies granted to each principal."],[2225,"its chain reaches a root trusted by the consumer;"],[2226,"its dates and usages allow the operation;"],[2285,"Its public certificate in `ca.pem`; this example uses the root created in the previous path."],[2224,"its public key matches the client's private key;"],[2346,"Its public key matches the one included in `device.crt`."],[310,"Its status contains the expected address."],[2223,"its subject and extensions identify the expected client;"],[25,"Just want to evaluate the platform?"],[1337,"Just-In-Time Provisioning (JITP) mode delegates provisioning to AWS instead of the connector doing it directly. When the connector detects the DMS is in `jitp` mode, it creates a JITP provisioning template in AWS IoT Core and attaches it to the registered CA certificate. This template is created or updated at the moment the DMS is created or updated 